nix-snapshotter#183: containers fail with "open /nix/store/...: not a directory".

Cause: containerd >= 2.2 reads the container's /etc/passwd and /etc/group through
pkg/oci withReadonlyFS, which first tries internal/fsview.FSMounts. FSMounts looks only at the
last mount of the list and, when it is a "bind" mount, opens that mount's Source as the root
filesystem, ignoring that a mount with a Target is a submount. nix-snapshotter returns the rootfs
overlay followed by one "bind" mount per closure path, sorted by path, so the last mount is the
closure path with the highest hash: if that path is a file (a writeText, the image's
config-*.json), container creation fails with ENOTDIR; otherwise /etc/group is read from a store
path instead of the rootfs. CRI calls it on every CreateContainer (WithAdditionalGIDs under the
default supplementalGroupsPolicy Merge), so whether an image works depends on its hashes.

Fix: emit the store path mounts with type "none" and the same "ro", "rbind" options. mount(2)
treats them as the same bind mounts, fsview does not claim the list (ErrNotImplemented), and
containerd falls back to mounting the whole list read-only and reading the real rootfs.

Applies to standalone upstream nix-snapshotter v0.4.0.

--- a/pkg/nix/snapshotter.go
+++ b/pkg/nix/snapshotter.go
@@ -383,8 +383,14 @@
 			pathsSeen[nixStorePath] = struct{}{}
 
 			log.G(ctx).Debugf("[nix-snapshotter] Bind mounting nix store path %s", nixStorePath)
+			// The "rbind" option makes this a bind mount; the type stays "none" because
+			// containerd >= 2.2 (pkg/oci withReadonlyFS, internal/fsview) treats a list
+			// ending in a "bind" mount as that bind's source being the whole root
+			// filesystem: it opens the last store path as the root, which fails with
+			// ENOTDIR when that path is a file (nix-snapshotter#183) and reads the wrong
+			// tree otherwise. An unknown type makes it mount the list instead.
 			mounts = append(mounts, mount.Mount{
-				Type:   "bind",
+				Type:   "none",
 				Source: nixStorePath,
 				Target: nixStorePath,
 				Options: []string{
--- a/pkg/nix/snapshotter_test.go
+++ b/pkg/nix/snapshotter_test.go
@@ -171,7 +171,7 @@
 		expectedMounts = append(expectedMounts,
 			mount.Mount{
-				Type:    "bind",
+				Type:    "none",
 				Source:  nixStorePath,
 				Target:  nixStorePath,
 				Options: []string{"ro", "rbind"},
 			})
